---
import Button from './gb/Button.astro';

const essay =
  'https://medium.com/@drensin/elephants-goldfish-and-the-new-golden-age-of-software-engineering-c33641a48874';
---

<section class="section section-tight essay" id="essay">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="headline">Why an elephant, and why a goldfish.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="essay-grid">
      <figure class="essay-figure">
        <img
          src="/main-graphic.png"
          width="1400"
          height="781"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          alt="Illustration of an elephant at a drafting desk holding a blueprint, a human engineer orchestrating the handoff, and a goldfish inspector with a magnifying glass"
        />
      </figure>
      <div class="essay-body">
        <p class="lead">
          The model comes from Dave Rensin&rsquo;s essay &ldquo;Elephants, Goldfish, and the New
          Golden Age of Software Engineering.&rdquo; It explains the reasoning behind the split:
          context is an asset when you design and a liability when you review.
        </p>
        <Button color="outlined" size="md" href={essay} target="_blank">
          Read the essay on Medium
          <svg viewBox="0 -960 960 960" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="m216-160-56-56 464-464H360v-80h400v400h-80v-264L216-160Z"></path>
          </svg>
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .essay-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    column-gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px);
    row-gap: 28px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .essay-figure {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    background: var(--md-sys-color-surface-container-low);
  }

  .essay-figure img {
    display: block;
    inline-size: 100%;
    block-size: auto;
  }

  .essay-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .essay-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
